note('Pass 20 recovered individual-token states by differencing adjacent prefix means. Diagnosed a problem in old gates: approximate bias units solved on mean activations were only ~0.68 at the median live body token, down to .18, and missed most body positions. New Fisher domain/phase keys and an exact-token constant separate med vs general across unseen probe states (e.g. L24 med median .88 vs general .26). Refusal/evaluation polarity grows from L17 to L24 even at identical prefixes; pass 21 edits incrementally transport that activation difference at three blocks, then apply medically and phase-gated Italian empathy and action preference corrections. Uses only matched activation contrasts and closed-form weight algebra.')